The thing about drinking from fountains early on isn't so much that it
is dangerous (which it is), but that it wastes benefits.

Some fountains are magical.  Magical fountains increase your stats.  If
you have low luck, which a starting character does, you get one stat
increased.  But with a higher luck (I think higher than 4), you get all
your stats increased.  I wait to quaff from fountains until I have a
blessed luckstone and lots of luck because I like free stat increases.
And I'm pretty sure that luck affects how likely you are to get a water
demon *and* a wish as opposed to an angry demon.

I think that trying uncursed amulets is a good thing too, and if it's
an amulet of change, oh well.  That's is easily corrected once you find
another amulet.

I think it is kind of funny that you thought nothing would stop you
once you had MR and resisted poison.  There is always reflection too,
unless you like burnt armor or being disintegrated by a black dragon.
I always feel naked until I get reflection.  Of course, I feel even
more naked unless I have MR, polymorph control, or unchanging.  MR is
first in importance for me, but reflection is a close second.

The one thing I guess I don't get is that you had all that trouble in
mine town and survived, but then you walked around blindfolded knowing
there was a "c" corpse.  If that were me I might decide to stop playing
after surviving the initial skirmish because I'd be too excited to
think clearly.  Otherwise I might make a specific point of waiting
until the corpse rotted before I did anything else.  YMMV, it works for
me.



